From f002513b2b6b0211bbfa0b7c8a1d67da4b37e7b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 16:33:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01146/11171] [outer-loop] Planner discipline: split powered
 multi-codex-call experiments (.371 exp4011 hit the 80-min wall-clock cap 3x)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The powered GAP-4 experiments make hours of sequential 600s codex calls and
repeatedly hit the conductor's 80-min hard cap (exp4011 failed 3x, ~4h burned).
The conductor's own design says split long experiments into write-script +
run-script; the planner emits monolithic long tasks instead. Added a
MANDATORY-NEXT-MILESTONE planner-discipline note so future milestones split
them. No running-system change — the cap is correct (idle hangs die at 10 min);
the fix is planner-side. exp4011 is non-critical (prior .370 result exists) and
3-fail-skips cleanly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
